# Git, branches, and PRs

## Branches

- Prefix as a path segment: `feat/…`, `fix/…`, `docs/…`, `chore/…`, `test/…`, `wip/…`.
- With a ticket key, put it first: `ABC-123-fix/short-slug`.
- Short, intent-shaped slug. Always lowercase.
- **Never** use the `cursor/` prefix. Cloud Agent runs default to `cursor/<name>-suffix`; rename before opening or updating a PR.
- Never commit to `main` or a release branch.

## Commits

- Conventional-commit subjects with an optional scope: `fix(map): …`, `feat(dashboard): …`, `docs: …`.
- Imperative subject. A body only when the why isn't obvious.
- One logical change per commit.
- Stage explicit paths (`git add <path>`). Never `git add -A`.
- Each commit must compile and pass the tests for the code it touches.
- Before any push, run the full validation for the touched area.
- Never force-push. Exception: a branch you own may use `--force-with-lease` after integrating remote commits you didn't write.
- Don't amend or rewrite published commits unless asked.

## Pull requests

- Title: `type: brief description`.
- Keep PRs small and focused. Break large features into several PRs.
- Follow existing conventions. Study similar code before implementing.
- Fill `.github/pull_request_template.md`: Why, Testing done, Notes.
- Never merge PRs, including `gh pr merge --auto`.

